---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../../lib/siteUrl';
---

<Layout
  title="Analytics Disclosure — Varve Docs"
  description="Varve's technical analytics disclosure: the small, consent-gated event inventory and the data Varve never collects."
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <article class="analytics-page">
      <h1>Analytics disclosure</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Website analytics records consented pageviews, referring site origins, and installer-link
        clicks using GoatCounter. Unknown consent fails closed. No remote tracking script,
        autocapture, session replay, analytics cookie, or visitor fingerprint is used. Unique
        visitors are not measured; repeated page loads count again.
      </p>

      <h2>Website events</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Event</th><th>Fields</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>website_page_viewed</td><td>normalized route</td><td>Understand which documentation and product pages are useful.</td><td>emitted</td></tr>
          <tr><td>website_download_started</td><td>release, platform, architecture, package type, release channel</td><td>Count installer-link clicks by route and package; not successful downloads or installations.</td><td>sent as website_download_clicked</td></tr>
          <tr><td>website_outbound_clicked</td><td>destination category</td><td>Legacy schema category.</td><td>not sent by this website provider</td></tr>
          <tr><td>website_contact_clicked</td><td>channel category</td><td>Legacy schema category.</td><td>not sent by this website provider</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Desktop events</h2>
      <p>
        The existing application event schema is listed below for reference. The website's
        GoatCounter account does not receive product-usage or diagnostics events. These remain
        separate application controls and provider configuration; their collection status is
        not established by the website analytics setup.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Event</th><th>Fields</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>app_launched</td><td>surface</td><td>Count opted-in product sessions.</td><td>separate application configuration</td></tr>
          <tr><td>document_created</td><td>blank, template, or import source</td><td>Understand activation without seeing the document.</td><td>separate application configuration</td></tr>
          <tr><td>feature_used</td><td>closed feature category</td><td>Prioritize features with meaningful adoption.</td><td>separate application configuration</td></tr>
          <tr><td>export_completed / export_failed</td><td>format and coarse duration or error category</td><td>Find export reliability and performance problems.</td><td>separate application configuration</td></tr>
          <tr><td>renderer_fallback</td><td>from, to, reason</td><td>Find platform-specific renderer fallback issues.</td><td>separate application configuration</td></tr>
          <tr><td>browser_demo_launched</td><td>entry source</td><td>Legacy usage-consent category.</td><td>not sent by this website provider</td></tr>
          <tr><td>browser_demo_desktop_download</td><td>release, platform, architecture, package type</td><td>Count installer-link clicks on the website demo route.</td><td>website click only; not product conversion</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Never collected</h2>
      <p>
        Documents, canvas pixels, screenshots, exported artwork, clipboard data, filenames, paths,
        project or layer names, user text, comments, URLs from designs, imported metadata, image
        hashes, geometry, generated code, AI prompts, raw exception strings, raw stacks, device
        identifiers, authentication identities, advertising identifiers, and arbitrary payload
        fields are prohibited by the schema and runtime privacy boundary.
      </p>

      <h2>Consent and transport</h2>
      <p>
        Website consent is separate from desktop usage analytics, diagnostics telemetry, and crash
        reporting. The client uses a bounded in-memory queue, never blocks editing or navigation,
        and discards pending events when consent is revoked or the process ends. The production
        website deployment maps the existing <code>varve.studio</code> switch to the private
        <code>varvestudio.goatcounter.com</code> account. Local and unconfigured builds remain
        endpoint-free. A new provider-specific consent choice is required; old refusals remain
        respected, and Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track always blocks collection.
        Session identification, individual-pageview storage, and demographic/device collection
        are disabled. Only aggregate counts are retained. Normalized routes omit fragments and
        all query strings except an allowlisted first-party campaign tag; some sections share
        the home category, so that category is not a literal homepage count. Referrers are
        reduced to site origins.
      </p>
      <p><a href={sitePath('/about/privacy')}>Read the full privacy policy</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .analytics-page { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 0; }
  /* Display typography: the bespoke hero ramp is page art, not a shared role. */
  h1 { color: var(--text-primary); font-family: var(--font-editorial); font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.75rem); margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  h2 { color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem; }
  p { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.1rem; max-width: 65ch; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.55; }
  th, td { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-default); padding: 0.75rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { color: var(--text-primary); }
  a { color: var(--text-link); }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { table { display: block; overflow-x: auto; } }
</style>
